<title>PORTUGAL: Yield eases on Portuguese 91-day bills.</title>
<headline>Yield eases on Portuguese 91-day bills.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield eased to 6.2678 percent, from 6.3983 percent previously, at the Treasury's sale of 91-day bills, the Bank of Portugal said.</p>
<p>The Treasury placed 27 billion escudos after initially offering 20 billion. The last such sale was on December 16.</p>
<p>--LISBON BUREAU 3511-3150035</p>
